---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Manual — Seriatim"
  description="How to install, find, route and uninstall Seriatim."
>
  <h1>Manual</h1>

  <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
  <p>
    Open the downloaded <code>.dmg</code>, run the <code>.pkg</code> installer
    inside, and restart your host. The installer places files system-wide and
    will ask for an administrator password once.
  </p>

  <h2 id="where-things-land">Where things land</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/Seriatim.component</code></li>
    <li><code>/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/Seriatim MIDI FX.component</code></li>
    <li><code>/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3/Seriatim.vst3</code></li>
    <li><code>/Applications/Seriatim.app</code></li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="finding-it">Finding it in your host</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Live:</strong> Seriatim appears as an instrument (VST3 or AU) in the plug-in browser.</li>
    <li><strong>Logic Pro:</strong> the instrument appears in the AU instrument list; <strong>Seriatim MIDI FX</strong> appears separately in the MIDI FX slot of any software-instrument track.</li>
    <li><strong>Reaper:</strong> appears as both VST3 and AU under Seriatim / Chaos of Zen.</li>
    <li><strong>Bitwig:</strong> appears as a VST3 instrument.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="driving-four-instruments">Driving four instruments in Live</h2>
  <p>
    Live does not offer a way to filter an internal plugin's MIDI output by
    channel — a track's <em>MIDI From</em> offers Pre FX / Post FX / a device,
    with no per-channel filter. Rather than routing one instance four ways,
    use one instance per voice and let the plugin do the splitting:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Four plugin tracks, each with its own Seriatim <strong>VST3</strong> instance
      (the AU's MIDI output is not offered as a routing source in Live).
    </li>
    <li>
      Four instrument tracks, paired one-to-one with the plugin tracks. Set
      each one's <em>MIDI From</em> to its partner plugin track's Seriatim
      device, and <em>Monitor</em> to <strong>In</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      On plugin track <em>n</em>, solo voice <em>n</em> (the per-voice
      <strong>S</strong> toggle). Solo suppresses event emission, so a soloed
      instance sends only that voice's notes.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Give the four instances different seeds for four independent parts, or
    leave the seeds equal for four voices of the same quartet split across
    four instruments.
  </p>

  <h2 id="uninstall">Uninstall</h2>
  <p>
    Mount the dmg again and run <code>Uninstall Seriatim.sh</code>, next to
    the pkg. Pass <code>--yes</code> to skip the confirmation prompt.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you no longer have the dmg, remove these paths directly (the app and
    plug-ins may also be user-level, under <code>~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins</code>
    instead of <code>/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins</code>):
  </p>
  <pre><code>sudo rm -rf "/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/Seriatim.component"
sudo rm -rf "/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/Seriatim MIDI FX.component"
sudo rm -rf "/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3/Seriatim.vst3"
sudo rm -rf "/Applications/Seriatim.app"</code></pre>

  <p><a href="/seriatim/changelog">Changelog</a> · <a href="/seriatim/download">Download</a></p>
</Base>
